<para><verbatim>embed:rst 
Inserts the reference `KVPs`_ from the graph at \ref dst into the graph at \ref src
:raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;` :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;`

With no \ref partFilter, the `KVPs`_ go straight to the very front/back (based on
\ref latest) of every root `section`_ of the graph at \ref src. With one, they instead
go at the earliest/latest valid index of every :cpp:class:`IfContentPart` the filter
accepts
</verbatim></para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>graphGroups</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The group of graphs to edit for each .ini file, modified in place </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>modType</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type of mod to fix <ndash/> only ever handed to <ref refid="class_a_g_remap_core_1_1_graph_inherit_1a2be93882177ebbd60607b432a1f5b8ec" kindref="member">partFilter</ref>. <bold>Nullable</bold> </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>modName</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The name of the mod to fix to. <bold>Default</bold>: <computeroutput>""</computeroutput></para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>The same groups that were passed in, after editing </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
